WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.690
The paper makes four contributions.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:07.460
First,

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:11.230
a generic framework that turns any fragment of an
algebraic language into a graph neural

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:15.000
network through context-free grammars.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:18.770
Second, it runs that framework on the ML-of-L-three
fragment and out comes G2N2,

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:22.540
a network that is provably 3-W-L.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:26.310
Third, it validates the rule set experimentally,

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:30.080
showing that the grammar reduction keeps
expressiveness while trimming redundancy.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:33.850
And fourth, across a broad battery of downstream tasks,

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:37.620
G2N2 beats the existing 3-W-L networks, often while
running faster.
